<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE DAVEfunc SYSTEM "DAVEfunc.dtd">
<DAVEfunc>
  <fileHeader name="AetherionFlightModel">
    <author name="Onur Tuncer" org="Istanbul Technical University"/>
    <author name="Caglar Ucler" org="Ozyegin University"/>
    <author name="Ahmet Gunes" org="Istanbul Technical University"/>
    <fileCreationDate date="2026-08-20"/>
    <description>
      Tabulated flight model of the Aetherion ducted-fan tail-sitter, generated from the Aeolion aerodynamic toolkit. Body axes are the contract frame aetherion_body_frd (x forward, y right, z down), the standard aeronautical body axis system of ANSI/AIAA R-004-1992. Moments are about the contract's moment_reference_point. See models/README.md for the normative specification and models/report/ for the technical report.
      
      VALIDITY. Incompressible, M &lt; 0.3: no Mach dependence exists in the generating methods. Single Reynolds number -- every table was generated at V = 25 m/s. Propulsor tables are AXIAL INFLOW ONLY, because the rotor-vane machinery is axisymmetric end to end; alphaDiskDeg is output as a validity monitor rather than faked as a table axis. Powered operation only: the rho n^2 D^4 group excludes n -&gt; 0, so windmilling and low-rotor-speed descent are outside the envelope.
      
      RATE DERIVATIVES. Measured at two perturbation amplitudes a factor of nine apart. The attached range and deep stall agree to four digits; roughly 20-30 degrees does not, differing by up to 196% with the SIGN not surviving. Across that band a linear rate derivative is structurally invalid -- the response is nonlinear over the perturbation range -- so those breakpoints are ABSENT rather than tapered, clamped or filled with a measured number, all of which would be fabrications. A lookup interpolates across the gap. The longitudinal pair (CZq, Cmq) additionally comes from the inviscid path and is a FLOOR: a pitch rate acts through the chordwise arm between the bound line and the moment reference point, which is zero on this configuration.
      
      LIMITATIONS. Post-stall values are limit-cycle means, not steady states. CLmax is an upper bound -- bubble bursting is not modelled. The tables are the ascending-alpha branch; hysteresis is not represented. Rate derivatives are tapered to zero over alpha 20-40 deg, a declared assumption rather than a computed result. Parasite drag covers body and duct only -- the wing's profile drag is already inside the force tables -- and omits the duct's separated drag at incidence, so aeroCD0 is a lower bound at high alpha. The aileron flap model is lift-only: no section pitching-moment increment, no gap leakage, no viscous decay at large deflection, so tabulated roll authority is an upper bound.
      
      
      UNCERTAINTY BOUNDS: read the label carefully. Where a table carries an uncertainty element, the one-sigma bound is the NUMERICAL CONVERGENCE SPREAD -- how far the damped iterate still wanders over its averaging window. It answers whether a cell has settled, and separates a converged condition (which carries no bound at all) from one still moving. It is NOT the physical unsteadiness of the flow. On post-stall cells this metric reads of order 1e-7 while the physical fluctuation, measured independently by an unsteady particle-wake cross-check at the same attitudes, runs at RMS-to-mean ratios of 3 to 40. The two differ by orders of magnitude because they measure different things: one says the solver has settled, the other says the real flow buffets. A consumer treating the emitted bound as physical uncertainty would conclude these loads are known to seven digits, which is false. Post-stall entries remain limit-cycle MEANS of a quasi-steady method, and their physical uncertainty is not represented in this file at all.
      INTERACTION VALIDITY. The fan-on-airframe tables (coupling*) were swept at ZERO SIDESLIP and are indexed by alpha and Tc only, but the buildup applies them at every beta. Their beta dependence is therefore unmeasured, not established as weak. They are also uniform-disk-loading and swirl-free, and past alpha 16 they are differences of two limit-cycle means: the effect is thrust-ordered and real, but its attribution to delayed separation is consistent with the data rather than established by it.
    </description>
    <reference refID="srcAeroMap" author="aeolion_aero_map" title="Airframe baseline map and reduced-rate derivatives (aero-map.json)" date="2026-08-20"/>
    <reference refID="srcAileron" author="aeolion_aero_map (aileron block)" title="Aileron increment sweep (aero-aileron.json)" date="2026-08-20"/>
    <reference refID="srcParasite" author="aeolion_parasite_drag" title="Body and duct parasite drag, friction buildup plus crossflow branch (parasite-drag.json)" date="2026-08-20"/>
    <reference refID="srcPropMap" author="aeolion_propulsion_map" title="Ducted propulsor over advance ratio (propulsion-map.json)" date="2026-08-20"/>
    <reference refID="srcPropVane" author="aeolion_propulsion_map (single)" title="Per-vane control increments (propulsion-singlevane.json)" date="2026-08-20"/>
    <provenance provID="genProv">
      <author name="Aeolion" org="models/build-daveml.py"/>
      <creationDate date="2026-08-20"/>
      <documentRef refID="srcAeroMap"/>
      <documentRef refID="srcAileron"/>
      <documentRef refID="srcParasite"/>
      <documentRef refID="srcPropMap"/>
      <documentRef refID="srcPropVane"/>
      <description>Generated from cached solver sweeps; see each documentRef. Nothing in the assembler computes aerodynamics.</description>
    </provenance>
  </fileHeader>
  <!-- Inputs. varID is namespaced for this file's structure; name is the Annex A standard parameter name. -->
  <variableDef name="angleOfAttack" varID="alphaDeg" units="deg" initialValue="0.0" axisSystem="body" symbol="α">
  </variableDef>
  
  <variableDef name="angleOfSideslip" varID="betaDeg" units="deg" initialValue="0.0" axisSystem="body" symbol="β">
  </variableDef>
  
  <variableDef name="trueAirspeed" varID="trueAirspeedMps" units="m/s" initialValue="0.0" symbol="V">
  </variableDef>
  
  <variableDef name="airDensity" varID="airDensityKgpm3" units="kg/m3" initialValue="0.0" symbol="ρ">
  </variableDef>
  
  <variableDef name="bodyAngularRate_Roll" varID="rollRateRadps" units="rad/s" initialValue="0.0" axisSystem="body" sign="+RWD" symbol="p">
  </variableDef>
  
  <variableDef name="bodyAngularRate_Pitch" varID="pitchRateRadps" units="rad/s" initialValue="0.0" axisSystem="body" sign="+NU" symbol="q">
  </variableDef>
  
  <variableDef name="bodyAngularRate_Yaw" varID="yawRateRadps" units="rad/s" initialValue="0.0" axisSystem="body" sign="+NR" symbol="r">
  </variableDef>
  
  <variableDef name="propellerSpeed" varID="propSpeedRevps" units="rev/s" initialValue="0.0" symbol="n">
  </variableDef>
  
  <variableDef name="aileronDeflection" varID="aileronDeg" units="deg" initialValue="0.0" axisSystem="body" sign="TED" symbol="δa">
  </variableDef>
  
  <variableDef name="vaneDeflection_Pitch" varID="vanePitchDeg" units="deg" initialValue="0.0" axisSystem="body" symbol="δP">
  </variableDef>
  
  <variableDef name="vaneDeflection_Yaw" varID="vaneYawDeg" units="deg" initialValue="0.0" axisSystem="body" symbol="δY">
  </variableDef>
  
  <variableDef name="vaneDeflection_Roll" varID="vaneRollDeg" units="deg" initialValue="0.0" axisSystem="body" symbol="δR">
  </variableDef>
  
  <!-- Constants, transcribed from the geometry contract by the assembler. -->
  <variableDef name="WingAreaM2" varID="WingAreaM2" units="m2" initialValue="0.188285585">
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="WingSpanM" varID="WingSpanM" units="m" initialValue="1.06287982">
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="WingChordM" varID="WingChordM" units="m" initialValue="0.177146637">
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="XmrpM" varID="XmrpM" units="m" initialValue="-0.2423">
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="YmrpM" varID="YmrpM" units="m" initialValue="0">
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="ZmrpM" varID="ZmrpM" units="m" initialValue="0">
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="DiskDiameterM" varID="DiskDiameterM" units="m" initialValue="0.203">
  </variableDef>
  <!-- Derived quantities. alphaDiskDeg and phiWDeg are VALIDITY MONITORS: they index no table, and exist so a consumer can detect that it has left the axial-inflow envelope. -->
  <variableDef name="dynamicPressure" varID="qbarPa" units="Pa" symbol="q">
    <calculation>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
        <apply><times/><cn>0.5</cn><ci>airDensityKgpm3</ci><apply><power/><ci>trueAirspeedMps</ci><cn>2</cn></apply></apply>
      </math>
    </calculation>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="advanceRatio" varID="advanceRatio" units="nd" symbol="J">
    <calculation>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
        <apply><divide/><ci>trueAirspeedMps</ci><apply><times/><ci>propSpeedRevps</ci><ci>DiskDiameterM</ci></apply></apply>
      </math>
    </calculation>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="angleOfAttackDisk" varID="alphaDiskDeg" units="deg" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Validity monitor: angle between the free stream and the rotor axis. The propulsor model is axial-inflow only.</description>
    <calculation>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
        <apply><times/><apply><arccos/><apply><times/><apply><cos/><apply><times/><ci>alphaDeg</ci><apply><divide/><pi/><cn>180</cn></apply></apply></apply><apply><cos/><apply><times/><ci>betaDeg</ci><apply><divide/><pi/><cn>180</cn></apply></apply></apply></apply></apply><apply><divide/><cn>180</cn><pi/></apply></apply>
      </math>
    </calculation>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="vaneDeflection_Bottom" varID="vaneBottomDeg" units="deg" axisSystem="body">
    <description>The bottom vane's own total commanded angle, from the mixing matrix. The per-vane tables are indexed by this, and the four contributions are summed.</description>
    <calculation>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
        <apply><plus/><ci>vaneRollDeg</ci><ci>vaneYawDeg</ci></apply>
      </math>
    </calculation>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="vaneDeflection_Left" varID="vaneLeftDeg" units="deg" axisSystem="body">
    <description>The left vane's own total commanded angle, from the mixing matrix. The per-vane tables are indexed by this, and the four contributions are summed.</description>
    <calculation>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
        <apply><minus/><ci>vaneRollDeg</ci><ci>vanePitchDeg</ci></apply>
      </math>
    </calculation>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="vaneDeflection_Top" varID="vaneTopDeg" units="deg" axisSystem="body">
    <description>The top vane's own total commanded angle, from the mixing matrix. The per-vane tables are indexed by this, and the four contributions are summed.</description>
    <calculation>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
        <apply><minus/><ci>vaneRollDeg</ci><ci>vaneYawDeg</ci></apply>
      </math>
    </calculation>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="vaneDeflection_Right" varID="vaneRightDeg" units="deg" axisSystem="body">
    <description>The right vane's own total commanded angle, from the mixing matrix. The per-vane tables are indexed by this, and the four contributions are summed.</description>
    <calculation>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
        <apply><plus/><ci>vaneRollDeg</ci><ci>vanePitchDeg</ci></apply>
      </math>
    </calculation>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="propellerThrust" varID="propThrustN" units="N" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Thrust from the propulsor tables, rho n^2 D^4 CT.</description>
    <calculation>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
        <apply><times/><ci>airDensityKgpm3</ci><apply><power/><ci>propSpeedRevps</ci><cn>2</cn></apply><apply><power/><ci>DiskDiameterM</ci><cn>4</cn></apply><ci>propCT</ci></apply>
      </math>
    </calculation>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="thrustCoefficient" varID="thrustCoefficient" units="nd" symbol="Tc">
    <description>T / (qbar S). Indexes the fan-on-airframe interaction tables. Degenerates as V -&gt; 0, hence the declared minimum speed.</description>
    <calculation>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
        <apply><divide/><ci>propThrustN</ci><apply><times/><ci>qbarPa</ci><ci>WingAreaM2</ci></apply></apply>
      </math>
    </calculation>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="reducedRollRate" varID="pHat" units="nd" symbol="phat">
    <calculation>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
        <apply><divide/><apply><times/><ci>rollRateRadps</ci><ci>WingSpanM</ci></apply><apply><times/><cn>2</cn><ci>trueAirspeedMps</ci></apply></apply>
      </math>
    </calculation>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="reducedPitchRate" varID="qHat" units="nd" symbol="qhat">
    <calculation>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
        <apply><divide/><apply><times/><ci>pitchRateRadps</ci><ci>WingChordM</ci></apply><apply><times/><cn>2</cn><ci>trueAirspeedMps</ci></apply></apply>
      </math>
    </calculation>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="reducedYawRate" varID="rHat" units="nd" symbol="rhat">
    <calculation>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
        <apply><divide/><apply><times/><ci>yawRateRadps</ci><ci>WingSpanM</ci></apply><apply><times/><cn>2</cn><ci>trueAirspeedMps</ci></apply></apply>
      </math>
    </calculation>
  </variableDef>
  <!-- Output variables the tables drive. -->
  <variableDef name="aeroCX" varID="aeroCX" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Airframe CX, power-off, controls neutral. Carries induced and wing profile drag; parasite drag is aeroCD0.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroCY" varID="aeroCY" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Airframe CY, power-off, controls neutral. Carries induced and wing profile drag; parasite drag is aeroCD0.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroCZ" varID="aeroCZ" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Airframe CZ, power-off, controls neutral. Carries induced and wing profile drag; parasite drag is aeroCD0.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroCl" varID="aeroCl" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Airframe Cl, power-off, controls neutral. Carries induced and wing profile drag; parasite drag is aeroCD0.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroCm" varID="aeroCm" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Airframe Cm, power-off, controls neutral. Carries induced and wing profile drag; parasite drag is aeroCD0.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroCn" varID="aeroCn" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Airframe Cn, power-off, controls neutral. Carries induced and wing profile drag; parasite drag is aeroCD0.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroDCX" varID="aeroDCX" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Aileron increment CX from the neutral configuration at matched alpha. The flap is carried in the section, so this attenuates through stall as the sections separate -- an inviscid lattice cannot show that.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroDCY" varID="aeroDCY" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Aileron increment CY from the neutral configuration at matched alpha. The flap is carried in the section, so this attenuates through stall as the sections separate -- an inviscid lattice cannot show that.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroDCZ" varID="aeroDCZ" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Aileron increment CZ from the neutral configuration at matched alpha. The flap is carried in the section, so this attenuates through stall as the sections separate -- an inviscid lattice cannot show that.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroDCl" varID="aeroDCl" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Aileron increment Cl from the neutral configuration at matched alpha. The flap is carried in the section, so this attenuates through stall as the sections separate -- an inviscid lattice cannot show that.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroDCm" varID="aeroDCm" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Aileron increment Cm from the neutral configuration at matched alpha. The flap is carried in the section, so this attenuates through stall as the sections separate -- an inviscid lattice cannot show that.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroDCn" varID="aeroDCn" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Aileron increment Cn from the neutral configuration at matched alpha. The flap is carried in the section, so this attenuates through stall as the sections separate -- an inviscid lattice cannot show that.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroCZq" varID="aeroCZq" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Reduced-rate derivative CZq. From the INVISCID path and a floor: a pitch rate acts through the chordwise arm between the bound line and the reference point, which is zero here, so the coupled path returns nothing and the chordwise load redistribution is absent by construction. Rows where the linearization failed are absent.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroCmq" varID="aeroCmq" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Reduced-rate derivative Cmq. From the INVISCID path and a floor: a pitch rate acts through the chordwise arm between the bound line and the reference point, which is zero here, so the coupled path returns nothing and the chordwise load redistribution is absent by construction. Rows where the linearization failed are absent.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroClp" varID="aeroClp" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Reduced-rate derivative Clp. From the COUPLED path, which carries the section model's post-stall lift slope. Rows where the linearization failed are absent.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroCnp" varID="aeroCnp" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Reduced-rate derivative Cnp. From the COUPLED path, which carries the section model's post-stall lift slope. Rows where the linearization failed are absent.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroCYp" varID="aeroCYp" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Reduced-rate derivative CYp. From the COUPLED path, which carries the section model's post-stall lift slope. Rows where the linearization failed are absent.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroClr" varID="aeroClr" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Reduced-rate derivative Clr. From the COUPLED path, which carries the section model's post-stall lift slope. Rows where the linearization failed are absent.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroCnr" varID="aeroCnr" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Reduced-rate derivative Cnr. From the COUPLED path, which carries the section model's post-stall lift slope. Rows where the linearization failed are absent.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroCYr" varID="aeroCYr" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Reduced-rate derivative CYr. From the COUPLED path, which carries the section model's post-stall lift slope. Rows where the linearization failed are absent.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="aeroCD0" varID="aeroCD0" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Parasite drag of BODY AND DUCT ONLY -- never the wing, whose profile drag is already inside the force tables. Friction buildup plus a slender-body crossflow branch.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="propCT" varID="propCT" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Thrust coefficient, vanes neutral, T / rho n^2 D^4.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="propCQ" varID="propCQ" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Shaft torque coefficient, Q / rho n^2 D^5.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="couplingCX" varID="couplingCX" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Fan-on-airframe increment CX from the power-off configuration at matched alpha. The aft fan induces a favourable gradient UPSTREAM of itself, over the wing; the momentum-theory slipstream is identically zero there and would report no interaction at all.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="couplingCY" varID="couplingCY" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Fan-on-airframe increment CY from the power-off configuration at matched alpha. The aft fan induces a favourable gradient UPSTREAM of itself, over the wing; the momentum-theory slipstream is identically zero there and would report no interaction at all.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="couplingCZ" varID="couplingCZ" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Fan-on-airframe increment CZ from the power-off configuration at matched alpha. The aft fan induces a favourable gradient UPSTREAM of itself, over the wing; the momentum-theory slipstream is identically zero there and would report no interaction at all.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="couplingCl" varID="couplingCl" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Fan-on-airframe increment Cl from the power-off configuration at matched alpha. The aft fan induces a favourable gradient UPSTREAM of itself, over the wing; the momentum-theory slipstream is identically zero there and would report no interaction at all.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="couplingCm" varID="couplingCm" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Fan-on-airframe increment Cm from the power-off configuration at matched alpha. The aft fan induces a favourable gradient UPSTREAM of itself, over the wing; the momentum-theory slipstream is identically zero there and would report no interaction at all.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="couplingCn" varID="couplingCn" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>Fan-on-airframe increment Cn from the power-off configuration at matched alpha. The aft fan induces a favourable gradient UPSTREAM of itself, over the wing; the momentum-theory slipstream is identically zero there and would report no interaction at all.</description>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="propDCCXvaneBottom" varID="propDCCXvaneBottom" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>PER-VANE increment CX from one vane's own deflection. Sum over the four vanes at their mixed angles -- NOT a sum over command modes, which was measured wrong by up to 33%. Evaluated at the bottom vane's angle.</description>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="propDCCXvaneLeft" varID="propDCCXvaneLeft" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>PER-VANE increment CX from one vane's own deflection. Sum over the four vanes at their mixed angles -- NOT a sum over command modes, which was measured wrong by up to 33%. Evaluated at the left vane's angle.</description>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="propDCCXvaneTop" varID="propDCCXvaneTop" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>PER-VANE increment CX from one vane's own deflection. Sum over the four vanes at their mixed angles -- NOT a sum over command modes, which was measured wrong by up to 33%. Evaluated at the top vane's angle.</description>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="propDCCXvaneRight" varID="propDCCXvaneRight" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>PER-VANE increment CX from one vane's own deflection. Sum over the four vanes at their mixed angles -- NOT a sum over command modes, which was measured wrong by up to 33%. Evaluated at the right vane's angle.</description>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="propDCCXvaneTotal" varID="propDCCXvaneTotal" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>PER-VANE increment CX from one vane's own deflection. Sum over the four vanes at their mixed angles -- NOT a sum over command modes, which was measured wrong by up to 33%. Summed over the four vanes.</description>
    <calculation>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
        <apply><plus/><ci>propDCCXvaneBottom</ci><ci>propDCCXvaneLeft</ci><ci>propDCCXvaneTop</ci><ci>propDCCXvaneRight</ci></apply>
      </math>
    </calculation>
    <isOutput/>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="propDCCYvaneBottom" varID="propDCCYvaneBottom" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>PER-VANE increment CY from one vane's own deflection. Sum over the four vanes at their mixed angles -- NOT a sum over command modes, which was measured wrong by up to 33%. Evaluated at the bottom vane's angle.</description>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="propDCCYvaneLeft" varID="propDCCYvaneLeft" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>PER-VANE increment CY from one vane's own deflection. Sum over the four vanes at their mixed angles -- NOT a sum over command modes, which was measured wrong by up to 33%. Evaluated at the left vane's angle.</description>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="propDCCYvaneTop" varID="propDCCYvaneTop" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>PER-VANE increment CY from one vane's own deflection. Sum over the four vanes at their mixed angles -- NOT a sum over command modes, which was measured wrong by up to 33%. Evaluated at the top vane's angle.</description>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="propDCCYvaneRight" varID="propDCCYvaneRight" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>PER-VANE increment CY from one vane's own deflection. Sum over the four vanes at their mixed angles -- NOT a sum over command modes, which was measured wrong by up to 33%. Evaluated at the right vane's angle.</description>
  </variableDef>
  <variableDef name="propDCCYvaneTotal" varID="propDCCYvaneTotal" units="nd" axisSystem="body">
    <description>PER-VANE increment CY from one vane's own deflection. Sum over the four vanes at their mixed angles -- NOT a sum over command modes, which was measured wrong by up to 33%. Summed over the four vanes.</description>
    <calculation>
